    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi we r having an issue with the sublimation heat press on line 4. the colors arent transferring right to the polyester, they look really faded and washed out even though we are using the right ink. can u help me figure out what to check?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The faint color on polyester is most likely caused by incorrect heat pressure settings, as polyester requires a specific temperature and minimum dwell time to properly bond with sublimation ink. I recommend verifying that your heat is set high enough to melt the polyester fibers, ensuring the pressure is even and firm across the whole imprint, and preheating the garment or polymer pad before pressing. If you are using DIC or similar white fabrics, you might also need to test your heat settings on a scrap piece first to confirm the optimal balance. Try adjusting the pressure slightly more or increasing the heat by 5-10 degrees, then re-test with a new garment.",
      "source": "target",
