    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "we checked the temp and the pressure seems fine on the gauges. the heat is definitely hitting the right numbers and the pressure is even. its like the ink just wont stick to the fabric properly, almost like it's disappearing during the press. could it be a problem with the gas in the ink or something else interfering with the transfer?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is unlikely the ink itself is \"bad,\" as this rarely causes fading unless the pigment has settled out. The most probable cause is that the hot gas generated by the sublimation ink is escaping through the opening of your heat press instead of being trapped under the item to melt into the polyester fibers. You should install or verify proper heat sealing (a hot tuck seal in the back) to create a tight, airtight seal. Additionally, check your exhaust fan; if it is blowing directly onto the load during the press, it could be exacerbating the gas escape or cooling the item prematurely.",
